  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nModels remain in good agreement that high pressure will dominate\nthe weather pattern over the Northeast into the weekend. This\nwill provide fair weather for the rest of the week with day time\nhighs near normal and cooler nights thanks to radiational\ncooling. A cut off low offshore of the Mid Atlantic will meander\nwell southeast of New England through Wednesday. A NE gradient\nwill tighten at times between this system and the high centered\nNW of of New England bringing periods gusty NE winds near the\ncoast and building near shore waves. By Thursday into the Friday\nthe low will pull east away from New England with a strengthening\nnortherly gradient. This could lead to a couple of breezy days \nThursday and Friday when winds could gust 20-30 mph. High\npressure then moves close to overhead going into the weekend\nallowing winds to slacken.",
